# -- WARNING: gitignore rules cannot un-track a file that is ALREADY tracked --
# .kiro/steering/server-info.md and .kiro/hooks/tbn-data-verify.kiro.hook were
# both tracked and published on origin/main until 10 Aug 2026. Same defect
# class as data/api_keys.json. Fixed via git rm --cached + a full history
# rewrite (git filter-repo) across all branches, force-pushed. History no
# longer contains any of: .kiro/steering/server-info.md,
# .kiro/hooks/tbn-data-verify.kiro.hook, data/api_keys.json,
# docs/TBN-Shango-Partnership-Agreement-v2.md, gen_ishaan_key.py. Verified via
# the GitHub API directly (contents endpoint returns 404 on all 3 branches for
# all 5 paths), not just local checks. This comment stays as a marker of what
# was done and why, in case anyone is tempted to re-add these files thinking
# the ignore rule alone is protection -- it is not, for a file already tracked.

